{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk","id":1544129,"title":"Mage in shadowrun/cyberpunk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-17T12:21:04-07:00","id":1544129,"title":"Mage in shadowrun/cyberpunk","content":"How would you adapt mage to the cyberpunk/shadowrun world of not so far dystopian future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:32:43-07:00","id":1544131,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I'd wait until <b>Anima</b> one of the Trinity verse games comes out. It's set in a Cyberpunk setting roughly fifty years into the future. Just steal everything that isn't nailed down. WoD and Trinityverse are fairly close so most of the heavy lifting is done on tech and rules. Then you can work on creating a interesting world.<br /> <br /> You should be able to buy copies of <b>Anima</b> in a couple of weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T16:58:53-07:00","id":1544156,"title":"","content":"Do you mean in terms of rules/systems/mechanics or in terms of setting details?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T23:40:08-07:00","id":1544184,"title":"","content":"Well mechanics and systems of Cyberpunk technology mainly. The game has some fun chrome too. Basically the hard part of technical rules will be done and the fun of politics and conflicts will be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-18-2024, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T00:35:04-07:00","id":1544186,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, that question was aimed at the original poster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T04:17:52-07:00","id":1544194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544156#post1544156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean in terms of rules/systems/mechanics or in terms of setting details?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both<br /> 1. Questions like: What happened to the traditions?<br /> 2. What happened to the technocracy?<br /> 3. Do implants still do paradox? and if not whats the new mechanical implant limitation?<br /> and so on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T13:07:53-07:00","id":1544222,"title":"","content":"If I'm adapting the M:t Ascension setting to Cyberpunk I first ask what does that do to the core of each group. I know you were asking the original poster Person of Great Importance and worth, but I'm tackling his question.<br /> <br /> Between Gothpunk and Cyberpunk I don't think the meaning/value of the Trads change. The Technocoracy is probably much more smug. The Desparates are already bitter anti-Post-Colonial types. But the advanced tech doesn't change the themes. A Space Opera game would bring far greater change because of possibilities of exploration and new worlds.<br /> <br /> A Cyberpunk setting, because implants and Cyber gear are things you see discussed in <b>Discovery </b>or <b>Popular Science </b>not edgy sci fi wouldn't risk paradox. The implant limitation would likely involve some character trait some attribute plus willpower divided by something. I'm sure <b>Anima </b>has an interesting idea about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-19-2024, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T16:38:19-07:00","id":1544238,"title":"","content":"If we're talking Shadowrun, the Order of Hermes probably has a place in the Technocracy, since hermetic study is a major, mainstream magical tradition that the megacorps love, and most frequently use hermetic mages to ward their high security areas from... ahem, deniable, magic-using assets. The TU might have also gritted its teeth and made overtures to the VAs and Etherites to get them back in so that they could manage more control over the new frontiers of the cyberpunk world. It probably wouldn't convince everyone in those traditions, but it might convinced enough to have also won back what are effectively two new branches (Magic-Tech workers and the Grid Overwatch Division/megacorp construction and control over the Matrix), plus the OoH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T18:19:05-07:00","id":1544367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544238#post1544238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking Shadowrun, the Order of Hermes probably has a place in the Technocracy, since hermetic study is a major, mainstream magical tradition that the megacorps love, and most frequently use hermetic mages to ward their high security areas from... ahem, deniable, magic-using assets. The TU might have also gritted its teeth and made overtures to the VAs and Etherites to get them back in so that they could manage more control over the new frontiers of the cyberpunk world. It probably wouldn't convince everyone in those traditions, but it might convinced enough to have also won back what are effectively two new branches (Magic-Tech workers and the Grid Overwatch Division/megacorp construction and control over the Matrix), plus the OoH.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for Shadowrun it's basically the end of Techies and Trads.<br /> <br /> Oops, Super Dragon-Gods appeared, and brought Magic to the eyes of the masses! Oh oh, now there's no more Ascension War. Mages in both Techies and Trads sign up towards one of the Megacorps to sell their talents for the highest bidding. Some are &quot;Wizards&quot; or &quot;Witch-Doctors&quot; or whatever else, some are &quot;Technomancers&quot;, but that's it. The Megacorps will eagerly employ any one of them, no discrimination based on their original backgrounds. <br /> <br /> We know quite a few of the Megacorps are under the thumb of a few great dragons, but it's even possible that the Trads and Techies would even start up a Megacorp of their own... But after the initial stages of shock, the &quot;Technocratic Union S&amp;A&quot; and &quot;Traditions S&amp;A&quot; won't be any more special than any other one of the Megacorps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T01:38:35-07:00","id":1544379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544367#post1544367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, for Shadowrun it's basically the end of Techies and Trads.<br /> <br /> Oops, Super Dragon-Gods appeared, and brought Magic to the eyes of the masses! Oh oh, now there's no more Ascension War. Mages in both Techies and Trads sign up towards one of the Megacorps to sell their talents for the highest bidding. Some are &quot;Wizards&quot; or &quot;Witch-Doctors&quot; or whatever else, some are &quot;Technomancers&quot;, but that's it. The Megacorps will eagerly employ any one of them, no discrimination based on their original backgrounds.<br /> <br /> We know quite a few of the Megacorps are under the thumb of a few great dragons, but it's even possible that the Trads and Techies would even start up a Megacorp of their own... But after the initial stages of shock, the &quot;Technocratic Union S&amp;A&quot; and &quot;Traditions S&amp;A&quot; won't be any more special than any other one of the Megacorps</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, someone's making those Gamma grade augmentations. I suppose Itx and the Progenitors have to learn to cooperate now.<br /> <br /> Of course, Shadowrun would also present some... dire tidings for diablerie and ancients' feeding on their progeny on the vampire corner, if you assume that they're linked to the same thing that HMHVV is. (Spoilers for Dark Terrors!) <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Surprise, every vampire has a bit of the corruption of astral space in it, and having them feed on each other acts as a conduit for a terribly powerful Horror!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:28:15-07:00","id":1544424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544379#post1544379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, someone's making those Gamma grade augmentations. I suppose Itx and the Progenitors have to learn to cooperate now.<br /> <br /> Of course, Shadowrun would also present some... dire tidings for diablerie and ancients' feeding on their progeny on the vampire corner, if you assume that they're linked to the same thing that HMHVV is. (Spoilers for Dark Terrors!) <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Surprise, every vampire has a bit of the corruption of astral space in it, and having them feed on each other acts as a conduit for a terribly powerful Horror!</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a neat idea.<br /> <br /> And the Wyrm could be at least one of these Horrors. The Neverborn in Oblivion could be another.<br /> <br /> It would also be funny to see Megacorps employing packs of Were-beasts and hiring them to manufacture fetishes. Glasswalkers and Ratkins will be kings. I do envision however a certain isolationist tribe pledging their services to a certain South American Naturalist Dragon-God-Emperor and living the best life they always dreamed of.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Horrors, the things that Stygia and the Dark Kingdom of Jade do in particular, could be a huge catalyst to awaken the Neverborn from their slumber.<br /> <br /> What about the Fair Folk thou? Could they walk again the Material Plane without the need of the Changeling Way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T16:43:58-07:00","id":1544439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544424#post1544424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a neat idea.<br /> <br /> And the Wyrm could be at least one of these Horrors. The Neverborn in Oblivion could be another.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is far, far too big for that. Even its Triatic Aspects are too big for that. Maybe the Urge Wyrms and Maeljin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would also be funny to see Megacorps employing packs of Were-beasts and hiring them to manufacture fetishes. Glasswalkers and Ratkins will be kings. I do envision however a certain isolationist tribe pledging their services to a certain South American Naturalist Dragon-God-Emperor and living the best life they always dreamed of. </div> </div> </div>You can't manufacture fetishes unless they're Weaver fetishes that look like devices. And you'd run into the issue of the builders being able to use them, but not many others having that capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of Horrors, the things that Stygia and the Dark Kingdom of Jade do in particular, could be a huge catalyst to awaken the Neverborn from their slumber. </div> </div> </div>Anything having to do with the dead or an afterlife is a giant stumbling block for SR. It has been categorically avoiding having to answer any questions about life after death for the entirety of its run, and capping off any discussions of ghosts and similar spirits with twee &quot;well, actually&quot; takes from Hermetics. &quot;It's not really the spirit of the dead, it's just the psychic impression left behind on energy patterns that think that they're the real person!&quot; gets old fast, and doubly so for ancestor spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the Fair Folk thou? Could they walk again the Material Plane without the need of the Changeling Way? </div> </div> </div>*Points to Court of Shadows* Answer's there, probably. I haven't read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T01:08:09-07:00","id":1544448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544424#post1544424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What about the Fair Folk thou? Could they walk again the Material Plane without the need of the Changeling Way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldnt changelings just be shadowrun elves, trolls etc?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T08:53:14-07:00","id":1544463,"title":"","content":"For this, I would strongly recommend the Storyteller's Vault supplement <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/366711\" target=\"_blank\">Bleeding Edge 2.0</a>. While it's Chronicles of Darkness and not World of Darkness, it's similar enough that you can draw a <i>lot </i>of useful material out of it. <br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts' worldview would be central here: it is, quite literally, what they were made for. The paradox is that in their worldview, they're the plucky underdogs standing up against the Man; so although their worldview is ascendant, <i>they </i>are <i>not. </i>On the other hand, much of their technology will have become mainstream; meaning that things that would today be VA Wonders are Instead mundane technology. This includes the netrunning decks of the Nexplorers, of course; but also the cybernetics of the aptly named Cyberpunks. Of the other Traditions, I'd expect to see the Cult of Ecstasy playing a strong secondary influence, as sex, drugs, and rock and roll are a big part of the &quot;punk&quot; part of cyberpunk. <br /> <br /> On the Technocracy's side of things, it would be the Syndicate that's ascendant, followed by Iteration X and then the Progenitors. The New World Order is surprisingly rather low in standing, as the cyberpunk genre tends to assume that formal governments have become fragmented and largely ineffective, leading to megacorps filling in the power vacuum. And given the mostly Earth-centric nature of the typical cyberpunk setting, the Void Engineers are the least important of the Conventions. Heck, not even the wilderness explorers in the Convention have much to do, as cyberpunk tends to deal primarily with urban sprawls. <br /> <br /> In terms of the Digital Web, memophores or Digital Web Entities (M20 pp.638\u2013639) should be a more significant thing, with more of them being like the ISOs of Tron Legacy: digital intelligences in their own right, not merely programs created by and serving humans; viable characters. The long sought Artifical General Intelligence turns out not to be artificial at all, but merely a natural part of the digital world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:15:50-07:00","id":1544507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544448#post1544448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldnt changelings just be shadowrun elves, trolls etc?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, not quite. Elves and Dwarves and Trolls and the rest are basically sub-species of humans in Shadowrun. In the game lore itself its as if some humans had the &quot;recessive genes&quot; of these sub-species for several millennia, and when the Moon got ascendant over Saturn under the age of Aquarius and then Magic went BOOM!, these genes that were dormant became active. People who were normal humans, became Elves or even Halflings overnight.<br /> <br /> Changelings however are human beings with a sort of &quot;alien parasite&quot; Fae Soul. The process of a Changeling being born is a spiritual one, the process for Shadowrun's other species of fantasy hominidae is magic-genetic.<br /> <br /> That's a consideration one would have to make for such crossovers thou. Are the Changelings the Dreams of the collective unconscious about the mythical past upon which these races roamed the Earth, and these dreams came to &quot;infect&quot; the dreamers, creating the Changelings? But what happens now that the &quot;real deal&quot; is back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T17:56:13-07:00","id":1544524,"title":"","content":"Tomayto, tomahto. That is, it doesn't really matter if changelings aren't exactly the same as the demihumans of Shadowrun; they're close enough. The only thing I'd consider doing would be to make it a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; setting where a metaphysical change prevents changelings from pretending to be human.<br /> <br /> Specifically, I wouldn't do Shadowrun verbatim; I'd do a combination of a cyberpunk setting tech-wise and a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; Shard from Mirrors for the supernatural stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2024, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T23:32:21-07:00","id":1544535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544524#post1544524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tomayto, tomahto. That is, it doesn't really matter if changelings aren't exactly the same as the demihumans of Shadowrun; they're close enough. The only thing I'd consider doing would be to make it a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; setting where a metaphysical change prevents changelings from pretending to be human.<br /> <br /> Specifically, I wouldn't do Shadowrun verbatim; I'd do a combination of a cyberpunk setting tech-wise and a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; Shard from Mirrors for the supernatural stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is in Shadowrun there are vampires and they are still hiding so mascarade still would be a thing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:17:58-07:00","id":1544548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544535#post1544535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is in Shadowrun there are vampires and they are still hiding so mascarade still would be a thing for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires would always do best to hide, no matter which is the scenario. The &quot;True Blood&quot; scenario is highly unlikely (for those that don't know, &quot;True Blood&quot; was a garbage TV series where a Japanese scientist invented synthetic blood and with that the vampires turned their existence revealed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:25:52-07:00","id":1544549,"title":"","content":"But hey, what about Paradox? Is it basically thrown out the window now? That's a rather... Permissive Consensus we have here.<br /> <br /> Quelsec, will you also be introducing the Dragon-Gods thing? Would they be on par with Antidiluvians - or perhaps even more?<br /> <br /> That also seems to be a good timing for the Antis to awaken from their slumber and start their ancient shenanigans<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544524#post1544524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tomayto, tomahto. That is, it doesn't really matter if changelings aren't exactly the same as the demihumans of Shadowrun; they're close enough. The only thing I'd consider doing would be to make it a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; setting where a metaphysical change prevents changelings from pretending to be human. <br /> Specifically, I wouldn't do Shadowrun verbatim; I'd do a combination of a cyberpunk setting tech-wise and a &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; Shard from Mirrors for the supernatural stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good take on it. So, all Demihumans will basically be magical beings by default, connected to the Dreaming <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:07:05-07:00","id":1544572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544549#post1544549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quelsec, will you also be introducing the Dragon-Gods thing? Would they be on par with Antidiluvians - or perhaps even more?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if i want a Cyberpunk (mascarade setting) or shadow run (in the open) one actually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:47:54-07:00","id":1544574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1544535#post1544535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is in Shadowrun there are vampires and they are still hiding so mascarade still would be a thing for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't hide, actually. That's part of why most governments can have open bounties on the Infected, more often than not. Or how there's an entire nation of Infected in West Africa (Asamando) that's rich as hell because they can get earth elementals to just port all the ore in the ground up to surface level, because being a vampire means you usually get spellcaster and conjurer capabilities (probably a good indicator that this wouldn't work out well with the WoD). Even the secretive Ordo Maximus is only hiding because they're a secret society that's used to it, but they got the lid blown off them when they tried to kill former Ordo member (and vampire who drinks other vampires) Martin de Vries and he fought back. In public. At a book signing, for a novel he wrote that was a thinly-veiled and embellished account of one of the times that he's fought the order. He wrote an entire series of novels like this, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T03:24:59-08:00","id":1546718,"title":"","content":"how would you handle implants for mage in a cyberpunk setting mechanically? Keep in mind there is still a limitation in the form of cyberpsychosis and implants arent the safest healthwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T04:05:27-08:00","id":1546719,"title":"","content":"For Shadowrun I'd probably tie up Essence with Arete. They aren't quite the same mechanically, but if the intent is to limit spellcasting with more cyberware because you are Ship of Theseus-ing your identity, it's the best fit imo. Narratively I probably would also use Essence to gauge how awake the Avatar is.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you want to play the TU, it could be interesting to lean into the opposite for them and make implants necessary Instruments - ie go full AdMech and machine spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T04:49:27-08:00","id":1546720,"title":"","content":"A good bit of this would mainly be decisions about what consensus will accept, in terms of which implementations of technology are commonplace or even mundane in a future setting. Anyone who's been running Virtual Adept characters in long-running chronicles set within contemporary settings has already had to deal with this, as advances in computer technology make much of the early material related to that tradition seem positively quaint. Especially when it comes to AI, some effects which would have been considered vulgar back when the game was introduced have become commonplace.<br /> <br /> One could even run with an odd twist involving <i>both </i>the Traditions and Technocracy losing some degree of control over consensus, the push and pull of the different factions giving rise to social and technological dynamics which <i>no </i>side anticipated. Both supernatural power groups could be finding it increasingly difficult to maintain an ideological hold over certain aspects of consensus, and neither wants to back off enough to let the situation stabilize. This assumes that deeply philosophical metaplots fit into the play style of a group, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T08:27:49-08:00","id":1546728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1546720#post1546720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good bit of this would mainly be decisions about what consensus will accept, in terms of which implementations of technology are commonplace or even mundane in a future setting. Anyone who's been running Virtual Adept characters in long-running chronicles set within contemporary settings has already had to deal with this, as advances in computer technology make much of the early material related to that tradition seem positively quaint. Especially when it comes to AI, some effects which would have been considered vulgar back when the game was introduced have become commonplace.<br /> <br /> One could even run with an odd twist involving <i>both </i>the Traditions and Technocracy losing some degree of control over consensus, the push and pull of the different factions giving rise to social and technological dynamics which <i>no </i>side anticipated. Both supernatural power groups could be finding it increasingly difficult to maintain an ideological hold over certain aspects of consensus, and neither wants to back off enough to let the situation stabilize. This assumes that deeply philosophical metaplots fit into the play style of a group, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowrun scenario is basically the end of Traditions and Technocracy and the end of the Ascension War. Both factions would simply offer their services to the highest bidder among the Megacorps, and the difference between them would just boil down to &quot;technowizards specialists&quot; and &quot;classic wizards specialists&quot; among the Megacorps special divisions. Shadowrun after all isn't the Supernatural secret conspiracy scenario of WoD, and what's more, &quot;magic&quot; is part of its &quot;Consensus&quot;. The very reason for the Technocracy to exists evaporates - and with the return of magic on the open, so does the reason for the Traditions to exist as an organization.<br /> <br /> It would be every Mage for himself, and the power structure of this world is based off primarily on the Megacorps and secondarily on the governments.<br /> <br /> I assume that many on the Sindicate and the NWO would assume positions of authority within said Megacorps and Govs, as would a smaller fraction from the other conventions (Big Farma for the Progenitors, &quot;Space X&quot; for the VE, big industries for Iteration X), and they wouldn't be shy about hiring Hermetics, Choristers, Kung Fu Akashics or whatever, who also would have no reason to say no. After that, past affiliations wouldn't matter, for the Megacorps competition structure is more important. That, and having to deal with all the Dragon Gods whimsical wishes, trolls, vampires and the rest of the bunch.<br /> <br /> The one group that I would be most interested however are the VA. This world would be a thematic park for them. I assume some would just accept the Megacorps paycheck thank you very much, but many others would become rebel anarchists trying to &quot;shove it to the man&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions, the ones that don't take a fat paycheck job, they would just simply return to be doing what they were doing before the Order of Reason's rise: closeting themselves upon their Ivory towers seeking their &quot;enlightenment&quot; and the rest of the world can go f* itself. Either way, it would become a non-issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-07-2024, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T12:14:51-08:00","id":1546739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1546728#post1546728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadowrun scenario is basically the end of Traditions and Technocracy and the end of the Ascension War. Both factions would simply offer their services to the highest bidder among the Megacorps, and the difference between them would just boil down to &quot;technowizards specialists&quot; and &quot;classic wizards specialists&quot; among the Megacorps special divisions. Shadowrun after all isn't the Supernatural secret conspiracy scenario of WoD, and what's more, &quot;magic&quot; is part of its &quot;Consensus&quot;. The very reason for the Technocracy to exists evaporates - and with the return of magic on the open, so does the reason for the Traditions to exist as an organization.<br /> <br /> It would be every Mage for himself, and the power structure of this world is based off primarily on the Megacorps and secondarily on the governments.<br /> <br /> I assume that many on the Sindicate and the NWO would assume positions of authority within said Megacorps and Govs, as would a smaller fraction from the other conventions (Big Farma for the Progenitors, &quot;Space X&quot; for the VE, big industries for Iteration X), and they wouldn't be shy about hiring Hermetics, Choristers, Kung Fu Akashics or whatever, who also would have no reason to say no. After that, past affiliations wouldn't matter, for the Megacorps competition structure is more important. That, and having to deal with all the Dragon Gods whimsical wishes, trolls, vampires and the rest of the bunch.<br /> <br /> The one group that I would be most interested however are the VA. This world would be a thematic park for them. I assume some would just accept the Megacorps paycheck thank you very much, but many others would become rebel anarchists trying to &quot;shove it to the man&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions, the ones that don't take a fat paycheck job, they would just simply return to be doing what they were doing before the Order of Reason's rise: closeting themselves upon their Ivory towers seeking their &quot;enlightenment&quot; and the rest of the world can go f* itself. Either way, it would become a non-issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds quite a lot like a situation in which sleeper corporate interests slipped the Syndicate's leash, likely as a result of being underestimated, took control of consensus (or &quot;the narrative,&quot; as they would call it,) and began &quot;normalizing&quot; magick by way of social engineering once they realized how useful it might be for their purposes. It's something I can see happening, and some technocrats probably have fever dream nightmares about something like that occurring. If that's too far-fetched, picture a situation in which AI results in self-aware manifestations of corporate entities in the umbra, which quickly become so absurdly powerful that neither faction can cope with them on their own terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-08-2024, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T19:10:09-08:00","id":1546784,"title":"","content":"Why, YES I have; Cyberpunk: 2020 has supplement-books, <i>Night's Edge and Grimm's Cybertales</i>: They basically R. Talsorian trying to get into the V:tM market. So, magic in that game-system, well, your D&amp;D first-level Magic-User is more powerful. Vampires are strong, especially older-ones and ones with lots of psychic-powers; however, the game-system is very, lethal. <br /> <br /> We actually played a Dark Ages game with Cyberpunk-rules. In the books, that have all the stuff you need like melee-weapons, leather and knight's armor (SP14). The magic, reminded me a lot of hedge-magic, just more difficult and more powerful, but takes longer to activate. <br /> <br /> One game, was more like the movie, <i>Push</i>, in which you had agents tracking down teenagers with psychic-powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T21:17:39-08:00","id":1546787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1546739#post1546739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds quite a lot like a situation in which sleeper corporate interests slipped the Syndicate's leash, likely as a result of being underestimated, took control of consensus (or &quot;the narrative,&quot; as they would call it,) and began &quot;normalizing&quot; magick by way of social engineering once they realized how useful it might be for their purposes. It's something I can see happening, and some technocrats probably have fever dream nightmares about something like that occurring. If that's too far-fetched, picture a situation in which AI results in self-aware manifestations of corporate entities in the umbra, which quickly become so absurdly powerful that neither faction can cope with them on their own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, AGI could have that effect indeed, if unleashed in the setting. You could actually have a Terminator + Magic post apocalyptic world to play with in that sense.<br /> <br /> But back to Shadowrun, the return of Magic to the world would be the end of the Ascension War, and a Consensus that would embrace both magic and ultra tech. The tech part would be quite a surprise for all the ancient beings waking up into this new world, and magic would quickly become a part of the day to day lives of common people just like tech already is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T17:13:44-08:00","id":1546883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1546718#post1546718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would you handle implants for mage in a cyberpunk setting mechanically? Keep in mind there is still a limitation in the form of cyberpsychosis and implants arent the safest healthwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use the Enhancements Background from M20 as a starting point for this, but I'd reskin the Permadox that comes with cybernetics as Cyberpsychosis instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T06:51:23-08:00","id":1547148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544129-mage-in-shadowrun-cyberpunk?p=1546883#post1546883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd use the Enhancements Background from M20 as a starting point for this, but I'd reskin the Permadox that comes with cybernetics as Cyberpsychosis instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes perfect sense. A couple of the Iteration X characters in Mage fiction seem to be suffering from exactly that, and it's described in a pretty interesting way. I'd even tend toward this particular &quot;flavor&quot; of Paradox flaw being not-uncommon among cyborgs in the standard world setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}